  "prefLabel": "Dec 203.03 Extensions of Time",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 203.03 Extensions of Time.\n\n(a) Except for postponements of hearings pursuant to Dec 204.10, a party requesting an extension of time shall make such request in writing before the expiration of the period originally prescribed.\n\n(b) A party requesting an extension shall make a good faith attempt to gain the consent of the other parties for the extension.\n\n(c) The committee shall grant a request for extension of time if:\n\n(1) The party making the request has demonstrated that circumstances would cause undue hardship or inconvenience unless the request were granted; and\n\n(2) The extension would not unduly delay the proceeding or adversely affect the rights of any party.\n\n(d) The presiding officer shall notify all parties of any extension of time granted.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A eff 4-25-08",
